# Line endings for files whose bytes are hashed.
# SECURITY: HistoryTest manifests chain SHA-256 hashes of earlier runs (NIST AU-10). A Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrote them to CRLF, so the chain broke (runs 2026-11-23_035621Z and _035628Z, marked
# invalid). Keeping these files LF on every checkout keeps the hashes stable on every OS.
HistoryTest/** text eol=lf
# Binary run artifacts (screenshots and other files) keep their exact bytes. The text rule above would otherwise
# rewrite any CR LF byte pair inside an image, corrupting it and breaking its manifest SHA-256 (NIST AU-10).
HistoryTest/**/*.png binary
HistoryTest/**/*.jpg binary
HistoryTest/**/*.jpeg binary
HistoryTest/**/*.gif binary
HistoryTest/**/*.webp binary
HistoryTest/**/*.pdf binary
HistoryTest/**/*.zip binary
HistoryTest/**/*.gz binary
